cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SWAT-SMAP ensemble Kalman filter data assimilation framework"
message: "If you use this framework, please cite the paper given under preferred-citation."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marshall
    given-names: "Sebastian R. O."
    email: smarsh46@jh.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Environmental Health and Engineering, Johns Hopkins University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0853-6200"
version: "1.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rushmarshall/mekong-swat-smap-enkf"
abstract: >-
  Data-assimilation framework for satellite soil moisture in SWAT2012: a Python ensemble
  Kalman filter that assimilates CDF-matched SMAP into basin-average SWAT soil moisture, with
  its parameter search and diagnostic analyses, and a Python driver for a Fortran SWAT2012
  build in which an ensemble Kalman filter updates soil-water storage in every hydrologic
  response unit inside the hydrological time loop, so the analysis propagates into routed
  discharge. Applied to the Mekong River Basin with SMAP products at 9 km, 1 km and 400 m
  over 2015 to 2024.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - data assimilation
  - ensemble Kalman filter
  - SWAT
  - SMAP
  - soil moisture
  - Mekong River Basin
